<!-- =======================================================
     01 / CONTEXT
     ======================================================= -->

<CaseSection
  number="01"
  label="Context"
  title="Working between interface design, product communication, and technical requirements."
  intro="During a remote UI/UX internship at Datacakra, my work moved across two very different product needs: visualizing a Smart Building proposal for a sales pitch and supporting the early requirements work behind a stalled RekMed–SATUSEHAT integration."
>
  <p>
    I joined Datacakra as the only UI/UX Design
    intern in a cross-functional internship batch
    that also included project management, frontend,
    backend, and quality-assurance roles.
  </p>

  <p>
    My direct design team was much smaller: myself
    and a company UI/UX Designer who acted as my
    supervisor.
  </p>

  <p>
    Because the internship was fully remote, progress
    was communicated twice each working day through
    Slack — once in the morning and again in the
    afternoon — to my supervisor and the Head of IT.
  </p>

  <p>
    The internship was originally centered around one
    project: helping continue the integration of
    RekMed with SATUSEHAT. While that work was still
    preparing for design involvement, I was assigned
    to another design task that could immediately
    support the business.
  </p>
</CaseSection>


