<!-- =======================================================
     06 / REFLECTION
     ======================================================= -->

<CaseSection
  number="06"
  label="Reflection"
  title="A useful interface designer needs to understand what happens after the interface."
>
  <p>
    The two workstreams taught me different sides of
    the same lesson.
  </p>

  <p>
    The Smart Building proposal required me to turn
    technical capabilities into an interface that
    could communicate value quickly to people
    evaluating a product.
  </p>

  <p>
    RekMed required the opposite direction: working
    inward from an existing interface to understand
    what data it collects, why that data exists, and
    how those decisions affect the people responsible
    for integration and implementation.
  </p>

